{
  "id": "COMPOUND:17084 - PROTEIN:1106",
  "verbalization": "Nyasicoside appears to have a shared target of Gamma-aminobutyric acid receptor subunit gamma-2 through multiple indirect pathways, all involving Jasplakinolide Z1 as a common mediator. The evidence suggests that Nyasicoside acts on different enzymes, including pim-3 and myosin light chain kinase 3, which are both targeted by Jasplakinolide Z1. This kinase is known to modulate GABA receptor activity, implying a potential mechanism by which Nyasicoside may influence GABA receptor function through this intermediate. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust, albeit indirect, relationship between Nyasicoside and the GABA receptor subunit gamma-2. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Jasplakinolide Z1 in linking Nyasicoside to the GABA receptor, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated.",
